Example: Supermarket Checkout System

The performance of a supermarket checkout system can be evaluated using several performance measures:

Average waiting time: The average time customers spend waiting in the queue before being served.
Average service time: The average time a cashier spends serving one customer.
Queue length: The average or maximum number of customers waiting in line.
Cashier utilization: The percentage of time a cashier is busy serving customers.
Throughput: The total number of customers served during a specific period.
Customer time in the system: The total time from a customer's arrival until they leave the checkout.

These measures help evaluate the efficiency of the supermarket checkout process and identify areas for improvement.
